#conversation file
version=0.1

question "Thanks for doing this. I know it's not easy." {
    tag=Normal
    answer=I almost didn't show up. I sat in my car for twenty minutes.
    answer=But I'm here. So. Let's just do it before I change my mind.

    question "Take your time. There's no rush." {
        tag=Normal
        answer=There's always a rush. There's always something in my head telling me to hurry up and get this over with.
        answer=Sorry. I don't mean to snap at you. I don't do this. Talk. Not like this, not out loud.

        question "Can you tell me a little about yourself?" {
            tag=Normal
            answer=Mara. Twenty-four. I sell books to people who mostly don't read them.
            answer=That's it. That's the whole resume. I don't really know what else you want from me yet.

            question "Let's start from the beginning, whenever you're ready." {
                tag=Normal
                answer=Okay.
                answer=God. Okay. Where does this even start.

                question "Were you ever formally diagnosed with anything?" {
                    tag=Normal
                    answer=Psychosis, eventually, once enough people had watched me long enough to agree on a word for it.
                    answer=Before that it was just "an episode." Like I was a TV show that had gone a bit strange for one week.
                    answer=I actually thought I was dying, the first time. Not going mad. Dying. My body just kept sending me these signals and none of them made sense.

                    question "What happened when you actually went to hospital?" {
                        tag=HospitalScene
                        answer=I hid under my bed for most of the first day. I genuinely thought that was a reasonable plan.
                        answer=It was a mixed ward. Loud, all hours, someone always crying two beds down. I tried to walk out twice. They stopped me both times.
                        answer=I remember lying there not totally sure if I was dead or just very tired. That's not a metaphor. I mean I actually wasn't sure.
                    }
                }

                question "What did the voices say to you?" {
                    tag=VoicesScene
                    answer=At first I thought it was coming from outside. Like someone was talking just past the window. I actually got up and checked.
                    answer=It took embarrassingly long to understand it was coming from inside my own head. You don't want that to be true, so you don't let yourself land on it.
                    answer=Mostly it just narrated me. What I was doing, how badly I was doing it. Sometimes it told me I was worthless and nobody would care either way.

                    question "Did anyone believe you, back then?" {
                        tag=Normal
                        answer=Not at first. My mom thought I was being dramatic. My roommate thought I was on something.
                        answer=One doctor actually laughed, not at me exactly, just -- surprised, I think. It still felt like being laughed at.
                        answer=Someone else's family called mine "dangerous." Said it like it was obvious. Like I was a dog that had bitten someone.

                        question "How did your mom find out how bad it really was?" {
                            tag=Normal
                            answer=She hugged me too hard. That's it. That's the whole story.
                            answer=I flinched and she grabbed my wrist before I could pull it back in time.
                            answer=We didn't talk for three days after. Then she just started leaving food outside my door, like I was something wild she was trying to coax back in.
                        }
                    }
                }

                question "What do you do now, instead?" {
                    tag=Normal
                    answer=Little mechanisms. Things I made up myself, in my own head, to argue back with the voice when it starts.
                    answer=Keeping the noise down helps. Real noise, I mean -- when everything's loud outside, it's louder inside too.
                    answer=I got back into drawing. It's not therapy, nobody's paying me for it, it just -- gives the day a shape. That's all I need some days. A shape.

                    question "That still counts. You know that, right?" {
                        tag=Normal
                        answer=I don't know anything, honestly. Not for certain.
                        answer=But thanks. I'll try to believe you, just for tonight.
                    }
                }

                question "What's the closest you ever came?" {
                    tag=NormalFace
                    answer=...
                    answer=I haven't said this part out loud before. Not once, to anyone.
                    answer=There was a night the voice wasn't just narrating anymore. It was very specific about what it wanted me to do.
                    answer=My roommate came home three hours early because her date cancelled on her. That's the only reason I'm sitting here right now. A cancelled date.

                    question "You don't have to say anything else if you don't want to." {
                        tag=NormalFace
                        answer=No, I -- I want to. I don't think I've ever gotten to finish this sentence before.
                        answer=I wasn't trying to disappear quietly. I think some part of me was hoping somebody would stop me before I finished.
                        answer=Nobody tells you how much of it is just... waiting. Waiting to be caught.

                        question "I'm glad she came home early." {
                            tag=Normal
                            answer=Yeah.
                            answer=Me too. Most days. Not all of them, if I'm being honest with you right now. But most.
                        }
                    }
                }

                question "Why did you do this to yourself?" {
                    tag=Normal
                    sets=Insensitive
                    answer=...
                    answer=Wow. Okay.
                    answer=I didn't "do it to myself" like I spilled a drink. Something in my own head told me to, and I believed it. That's not the same thing.

                    question "Sorry. That came out wrong." {
                        tag=Normal
                        ending
                        ending_text=Mara said it was fine. It wasn't fine.
                        ending_text=She kept answering. Shorter every time.
                        ending_text=By the end she was just watching the door.
                        answer=It's fine. Can we just get through the rest of this?
                    }
                }

                question "What was actually going on for you, before?" {
                    tag=Normal
                    sets=Caring
                    answer=Before what. Before all of it, or before the specific night you're too polite to ask about yet.
                    answer=Fine. Before. I was failing out of school. My parents were splitting up and both insisting, separately, that they weren't.
                    answer=And underneath all of it, quietly, this feeling that I was being watched and narrated and judged by something that was never going to stop.

                    question "What did it feel like, right before?" {
                        tag=Normal
                        answer=Static. Like every bad thing about myself turned up to the same volume at once, all screaming together, and then that voice underneath all of it agreeing with every word.
                        answer=And then, right before -- it went quiet. For a second. Just one second.
                        answer=Nobody tells you that's the addictive part. Not the pain. The quiet.

                        question "And after?" {
                            tag=Normal
                            answer=Guilty. Immediately. Every single time, no exceptions, ever.
                            answer=And relieved, which somehow made the guilt so much worse. You're not supposed to feel relieved about this. I still don't know what to do with that.

                            question "Did anyone know, back then?" {
                                tag=Normal
                                answer=Not for a long time. I got good at it. Sleeves, excuses, changing the subject a half-second before anyone looked too close.
                                answer=You get scarily good at lying to people who love you. Nobody warns you about that part either.

                                question "Who found out first?" {
                                    tag=Normal
                                    answer=My roommate. She saw my arm when I forgot to lock the bathroom door. Just for a second, but a second was enough.
                                    answer=I told her it was the cat. We don't have a cat. We have never had a cat.
                                    answer=She didn't believe me for one second. She just sat down on the floor next to me and didn't say anything at all.

                                    question "That sounds like it mattered." {
                                        tag=Normal
                                        answer=It did. More than she'll ever know, because I never actually told her that either.
                                        answer=Nobody had ever just stayed before. Everyone else tried to fix it right there on the spot, like I was a problem to be solved before dinner got cold.

                                        question "Do you still hear it, now?" {
                                            tag=NormalFace
                                            answer=Sometimes. I'm not going to sit here and lie to you and say it's gone.
                                            answer=Quieter, though. It doesn't get to drive anymore, it just sits in the back seat, muttering.
                                            answer=I don't think it ever fully leaves. I've stopped waiting to win some final fight against it and started just -- managing it. Day by day. Barely, some days. But every day, so far.

                                            question "Thank you for telling me that." {
                                                tag=NormalFace
                                                answer=Thank you for actually listening. Really listening, not just waiting for your turn to say something comforting back.
                                                answer=Most people ask so they can stop feeling awkward about not having asked. You didn't do that. You let it be uncomfortable.

                                                question "I want to know. What would actually help you right now?" {
                                                    tag=NormalFace
                                                    ending
                                                    ending_text=Mara is still here.
                                                    ending_text=Not fixed. Not finished. Not okay, not really. Still here.
                                                    ending_text=Sometimes that's what a better question actually buys someone.
                                                    answer=Honestly? This. Somebody asking, and then actually staying long enough to hear the answer. And believing me while I gave it.
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                question "I think that's all I need to ask." {
                    tag=Normal
                    ending
                    requires_not=Caring
                    ending_text=Mara thanked me and left the way she came in -- guarded, unreadable.
                    ending_text=I don't know what happened to her after that.
                    ending_text=I keep thinking about the questions I didn't ask.
                    answer=Okay. Thank you for your time.
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
